#! ia 1.0

@cardinality one
  meaning
    says "At most one distinct target; a must obligation also requires its presence."
    answers "Is the row limited to at most one distinct target?"
  data
    order 0

@cardinality one-or-more
  meaning
    says "No upper bound; a must obligation requires at least one distinct target."
    answers "May the row have several distinct targets?"
  data
    order 1

@cardinality optional
  meaning
    says "Zero or one distinct target, including when the schema row uses must."
    answers "May the row have no target even when it says must?"
  data
    order 2

